---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import CallToBook from "../components/CallToBook.astro";
import { site } from "../config/site";

const flyerPerks = [
  "Free decals and windshield banners",
  "Sponsorship opportunities",
  "Discounts at various shops",
  "Events, meets, and cruises",
  "Community, networking, and support",
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Team Battle Ready | Killeen Car Club and Gaming Trailer"
  description="Team Battle Ready is a Central Texas car club and a mobile gaming trailer serving Killeen and Fort Hood. Play, connect, build, belong."
>
  <PageHero eyebrow="The crew" title="Cars at night. Controllers after." crumb="About">
    <p>
      Team Battle Ready is Joe Bonilla’s Central Texas crew. The car club came with the name. The gaming trailer is already loaded and rolling under the same four words.
    </p>
  </PageHero>

  <article class="section" style="padding-top: 0.5rem">
    <div class="wrap grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Two lanes, one mark</h2>
        <p>
          Play is the room: consoles, a coach, and a cabin that is already loaded. Connect is the crew, the unit, and the driveway full of people who showed up. Build is the trailer, the shop time, and the habit of finishing what you started. Belong is Killeen and Fort Hood having a place that is theirs to host.
        </p>
        <p>
          The trailer side is a climate-controlled game room for birthdays, units, schools, and anybody else who would rather have 24 players in a cabin than one TV in a garage. The club side is meets, cruises, and cars that look like they belong on a night poster. Booking a party does not sign you into the club. Following the club does not reserve the trailer. They share a name on purpose.
        </p>
        <h2>Who is on the crew</h2>
        <p>
          A second adult on youth events is the operating plan, not a claim that the roster is hired.
        </p>
        <aside class="memorial">
          <p class="eyebrow">In memory</p>
          <p>
            <span class="memorial-name">CW4 (Ret.) Luis Bonilla</span>
            — Rangers Lead the Way. #RLTW
          </p>
        </aside>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="poster">
          <p class="eyebrow">B4TTL3 · Central Texas car club</p>
          <p class="poster-title metal">Team Battle Ready</p>
          <img class="brand-logo brand-logo-plate" src={site.logo.plate} alt="B4TTL3" width="2096" height="944" />
          <ul class="poster-values">
            {site.values.map((value) => <li>{value}</li>)}
          </ul>
          <p class="poster-sponsor">{site.tagline}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel" style="margin-top: 0.8rem">
          <h2 class="metal" style="font-size: 1.7rem">From the launch flyer</h2>
          <p class="muted" style="margin-top: 0.5rem">Member benefits the flyer lists for the car club. These perks are not included with a trailer booking.</p>
          <ul class="checks">
            {flyerPerks.map((perk) => <li>{perk}</li>)}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="wrap prose" style="margin-top: 2rem">
      <h2>Find the crew</h2>
      <p>
        Team Battle Ready is a <a href={site.parent.href} rel="noopener noreferrer">Lead the Way Logistics & IT</a> offering.
      </p>
      <p>
        Instagram: {site.instagram.map((account, index) => (
          <>
            <a href={account.href} rel="noopener noreferrer">{account.handle}</a>
            {index === 0 ? " and " : ""}
          </>
        ))}.
      </p>
      <p><CallToBook /></p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
